Rolling up a thousand heaps of snow.
The land is beautiful as a painting;
How many great men arose in that time!
I recall Gongjin in his prime:
Little Qiao had just become his bride;
His bearing was heroic and vigorous.
With feather fan and silk sash,
He laughed and talked
While enemy ships burst into flame and vanished.
If my spirit visited that ancient state,
Wouldn't they mock me for being too sentimental,
Having my hair turned white so early?
Human life is like a dream;
I raise a cup to offer libation to the moon over the river."}

{
  "translation": "The Yangtze flows east, its waves washing away all the heroic figures of a thousand years. On the western side of the old fortifications, people say this is Red Cliff, where Zhou Yu of the Three Kingdoms once stood tall. Jagged rocks pierce the sky, startling waves crash against the shore, churning up a thousand piles of snow. The land and water are like a painting; how many heroes graced this brief moment in time! I recall the days of Gongjin—when Xiao Qiao had just married him—in his majestic vigor. With a feather fan and silk headband, he laughed and talked as enemy ships turned to ash and smoke. Though my spirit roams through the ancient kingdom, sentimental feelings make me laugh at myself for growing gray hair too soon. Life here is but a dream; I pour a cup of wine to honor the moon on the river."
}

{
