Rustling in bamboo: washerwomen returning home;
Stirring lotuses: fishing boats coming down the stream.
Let spring's fragrance fade as it will;
Here, the recluse can easily choose to dwell.

A new song, a cup of wine;
Last year's weather, the old pavilion and terrace.
When will the setting sun return?

Helplessly, the flowers fall away;
As if recognized before, the swallows come back.
Alone I linger on the fragrant path in the small garden.

