{
  "translation": "Ten years: life and death, both lost in vast uncertainty. Though I do not strive to remember, how could I forget? Her lonely grave lies a thousand miles away; nowhere can I voice this desolate grief. Even if we should meet again, she would hardly know me: my face covered in dust, my hair white as frost.\n\nLast night, in a dim dream, I suddenly returned home. Through the small lattice window, she was dressing her hair. We gazed at each other, speechless, only endless tears flowing down. I imagine that every year’s most heartbreaking place will be under the bright moon, on the mound of short pines."
}

