message.content:
{
"translation": "A thousand years of mountains and rivers stand, / Yet nowhere to seek the hero Sun Zhongmou. / The dance terraces and song stages have vanished; / Their romantic grace was swept away by wind and rain. / Beneath the slanting sun, among grass and trees, / In common lanes and alleys, people say that Ji Nu once lived. / I recall those years: golden spears and iron horses, / His spirit swallowing ten thousand miles like a tiger. / But Yuanjia’s hasty campaign aimed to seal Langju Mountain, / Only earning panicked glances toward the north. / Forty-three years have passed; looking out, I still remember / The beacon fires along the road to Yangzhou. / How can one bear to look back? / Beneath the shrine of Foli, crows cry and folk drums beat. / Who will ask, as with Lian Po in his old age, if he can still eat well?"
}

